# MAPAF Grafana Integration

## Overview

MAPAF integrates with Grafana through InfluxDB to provide real-time visualization of k6 performance metrics.

Architecture:

```text
k6
↓
InfluxDB
↓
Grafana
↓
MAPAF Performance Dashboard
```

## Components

### k6

Responsible for:

* Smoke Tests
* Load Tests
* Stress Tests
* Soak Tests

### InfluxDB

Stores:

* Request Metrics
* Latency Metrics
* Error Metrics
* Virtual User Metrics

### Grafana

Visualizes:

* Response Time
* Error Rate
* Request Rate
* Throughput
* Virtual Users

## Local Setup

Start InfluxDB:

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name influxdb \
  -p 8086:8086 \
  influxdb:1.8
```

Start Grafana:

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name grafana \
  -p 3000:3000 \
  grafana/grafana
```

Grafana URL:

```text
http://localhost:3000
```

Default Login:

```text
admin
admin
```

## Datasource Configuration

Type:

```text
InfluxDB
```

URL:

```text
http://host.docker.internal:8086
```

Database:

```text
k6
```

## Dashboard

Dashboard Name:

```text
MAPAF Performance Dashboard
```

Purpose:

Provide visibility into application performance during test execution.

